#: ../../source/from2_README.md:1
msgid "experimental"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:3
msgid ""
"`from2` is a high-level module for creating readable streams that "
"properly handle backpressure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:5
msgid ""
"Convience wrapper for [readable-stream](http://github.com/isaacs"
"/readable-stream)'s `ReadableStream` base class, with an API lifted from "
"[from](http://github.com/dominictarr/from) and "
"[through2](http://github.com/rvagg/through2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:11
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:13
msgid "[![from2](https://nodei.co/npm/from2.png?mini=true)](https://nodei.co/npm/from2)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:13
msgid "from2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:15
msgid "`stream = from2([opts], read)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:17
msgid ""
"Where `opts` are the options to pass on to the `ReadableStream` "
"constructor, and `read(size, next)` is called when data is requested from"
" the stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:20
msgid "`size` is the recommended amount of data (in bytes) to retrieve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:21
msgid "`next(err)` should be called when you're ready to emit more data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:23
msgid ""
"For example, here's a readable stream that emits the contents of a given "
"string:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:50
msgid "`stream = from2.obj([opts], read)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:52
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Shorthand for `from2({ objectMode: true }, read)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:54
msgid "`createStream = from2.ctor([opts], read)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:56
msgid ""
"If you're creating similar streams in quick succession you can improve "
"performance by generating a stream **constructor** that you can reuse "
"instead of creating one-off streams on each call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:60
msgid ""
"Takes the same options as `from2`, instead returning a constructor which "
"you can use to create new streams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:63
msgid "See Also"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:65
msgid ""
"[from2-array](https://github.com/binocarlos/from2-array) - Create a from2"
" stream based on an array of source values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/from2_README.md:66
msgid ""
"[from2-string](https://github.com/yoshuawuyts/from2-string) - Create a "
"stream from a string. Sugary wrapper around from2."
msgstr ""

